From 78b4298cfb1a5298f8b27c53d976874560c8f737 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bot <bot@example.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:03:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] direct3d11: support dynamic swapchain transform

Read an optional video_orientation_t transform from the WinRT
IDXGISwapChain via GUID_SWAPCHAIN_TRANSFORM private data, compose it
with the stream's native orientation, and update the D3D11 quad vertex
coordinates and display placement dynamically without reloading media or
tearing down the vout pipeline.

Also fix SetupQuadFlat 90/270/180-degree coordinate calculations for
padded or cropped textures, prevent double-rotation of direct-rendered
subpicture formats when scaling subtitles to a rotated output, pass the
rotated source format to spu_Render() so ASS/libass and text subtitles
keep the right aspect ratio, and scale bitmap subtitles (PGS/VobSub)
uniformly while anchoring bottom-half cues to the bottom edge when the
output orientation is swapped relative to the subtitle canvas.

Added for libvlc tag 3.0.23.
